{
 "id": "2026-10-25-birthday-paradox",
 "topic": "birthday problem: 23 people give a 50.7% chance of a shared birthday",
 "subject": "statistics",
 "hook_type": "visual surprise",
 "caption": "23 people don't make 23 chances for a shared birthday, they make 253 pairs. Multiply out the chance that nobody matches and you get 0.493, so a match is 50.7% likely (99.9% with 70 people).\n\nSend this to the group chat with the most people in it.\n\n#statistics #probability #math #birthdayparadox #combinatorics #datascience #stem #learnmath",
 "cover_at": 1.0,
 "hook": "Watch a 1-in-365 chance become a coin flip with just 23 people.",
 "sub": "The birthday problem.",
 "beats": [
  {
   "text": "Ignoring leap years, with every day equally likely, two people share a birthday with probability $1/365$.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "p2",
     "tex": [
      "P(\\text{2 match})",
      "=",
      "\\frac{1}{365}",
      "\\approx 0.27\\%"
     ],
     "size": 62,
     "at": [
      0,
      3.8
     ],
     "colors": {
      "2": "blue"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "So with 23 people, naive scaling suggests about 23 times that: roughly 6%.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "naive",
     "tex": [
      "23 \\times \\frac{1}{365}",
      "\\approx",
      "6.3\\%",
      "\\;?"
     ],
     "size": 70,
     "next_to": "p2",
     "side": "down",
     "buff": 0.8,
     "colors": {
      "2": "red",
      "3": "red"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "But a match needs a pair of people, not one person. Count the pairs:",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "pairs",
     "tex": [
      "\\binom{23}{2}",
      "=",
      "\\frac{23 \\cdot 22}{2}",
      "=",
      "253"
     ],
     "size": 70,
     "next_to": "naive",
     "side": "down",
     "buff": 0.9,
     "colors": {
      "4": "yellow"
     }
    },
    {
     "flash": "pairs"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "253 pairs, each a chance to match. To get the exact answer, compute the opposite: nobody matches.",
   "do": [
    {
     "circle": "pairs"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "do": [
    {
     "clear": true
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Person by person, each one must avoid every birthday already taken.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "none",
     "tex": [
      "P(\\text{no match})"
     ],
     "size": 84,
     "at": [
      0,
      4.2
     ]
    },
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "prod",
     "tex": [
      "=",
      "\\frac{365}{365}",
      "\\cdot",
      "\\frac{364}{365}",
      "\\cdot",
      "\\frac{363}{365}",
      "\\cdots",
      "\\frac{343}{365}"
     ],
     "size": 64,
     "next_to": "none",
     "side": "down",
     "buff": 0.6,
     "colors": {
      "7": "teal"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "The 23rd person has 343 free days out of 365. Now multiply all 23 fractions.",
   "do": [
    {
     "indicate": "prod",
     "color": "teal"
    },
    {
     "sfx": "riser"
    },
    {
     "morph": "prod",
     "into": {
      "make": "tex",
      "tex": [
       "\\approx 0.493"
      ],
      "size": 110,
      "next_to": "none",
      "side": "down",
      "buff": 0.6
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "So a shared birthday is more likely than not.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "ans",
     "tex": [
      "P(\\text{match})",
      "\\approx",
      "1 - 0.493",
      "=",
      "50.7\\%"
     ],
     "size": 58,
     "at": [
      0,
      0.4
     ],
     "colors": {
      "4": "green"
     }
    },
    {
     "sfx": "ding"
    },
    {
     "make": "box",
     "name": "ba",
     "around": "ans",
     "color": "green"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "With 70 people, the same calculation gives 99.9%.",
   "do": [
    {
     "make": "tex",
     "name": "n70",
     "tex": [
      "n = 70:",
      "\\;",
      "99.9\\%"
     ],
     "size": 84,
     "next_to": "ans",
     "side": "down",
     "buff": 0.9,
     "colors": {
      "2": "green"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "do": [
    {
     "clear": true
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Pairs grow like $n^2/2$, not $n$. That's why coincidences are far more common than intuition says.",
   "do": [
